  "prompt": "Build the v4 Film Grain tile as a dependency-free, reusable photographic grain overlay. Keep its exact 200×150px rounded dusk cover at 86,28 in the 372×264px stage, with the original border, 20% black wash and all 213 supplied grain primitives in their original order. Use the unchanged original SVG payloads without overriding intrinsic SVG dimensions. Animate the complete original seeded four-sample bell-noise field at 8fps, including every dust mark and periodic scratch, over the approved local photo. Keep the original intensity model, seed, frame indexing and 150×intensity alpha. Full view retains the complete 368×268px field, native 0–100 intensity range, frame readout and licensed archGrid photo in a readable 400×448px composition. Space freezes/resumes; R generates a new frame. Reduced motion starts with the native reference still and uses deliberate new frames plus interruptible 150ms opacity feedback. Keep all frame buffers, native range and keyboard behavior, physical touch scrolling, owned cancellation, queued intent and independent caller/viewport holds. The shell owns the controls. Export complete photo/font data and attribution without runtime dependencies.",
